	$("#commentsaboutthismap")
	.html("This partition of Brussels and its surroundings (Former Province of Brabant) is obtained by the <b>application of a community detection algorithm (The Louvain method) on nighttime-only phone calls</b> between towers located in the area. Each tower (aggregation of antennas located on the same structure) is represented by a cell constituted by the area closest to this tower. Each community can here be considered as an interaction basin in terms of communications. 4 communities are illustrated here, obtained with a resolution parameter equal to 1.4. Whatever the number of communities chosen, each of them is quite surprisingly contiguous: proximity matters even for non-physical communications.<br><br>Communities are displayed here as a <b>chorochromatic map</b>, each community being represented in a single color.<br><br>Note that one of the four communities is constituted by a single cell located in the Pentagon, the city center of Brussels, as the major part of calls from and to this cell are internal calls. One community is centered on the eastern part of the Brussels Capital Region, excluding parts of the Region being on the western bank of the Brussels-Charleroi Canal, but including towers located in some other municipalities at the south (Drogenbos, Linkebeek or Sint-Genesius-Rode; municipalities with language facilities) or at the east (Tervuren). The limit between the two other communities broadly follows the linguistic border between Walloon Brabant and Flemish Brabant.") ;
	
	$("#downloadthismap")
	.html("To download a map, make a right-click on the format (.svg or .png), select 'save as', and specify the directory where you want to save it.<br><br><b>Communities only<br>(chorochromatic map)</b><br><a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4.svg" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4.svg" + "><button type=button" + ">.svg</button></a> & <a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4.png" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4.png" + "><button type=button" + ">.png</button></a><br><br><b>Communities on a layer of population density</b><br><a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4denspop.svg" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4denspop.svg" + "><button type=button" + ">.svg</button></a> & <a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4denspop.png" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4denspop.png" + "><button type=button" + ">.png</button></a><br><br><b>Communities on a layer of built-up density</b><br><a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4densbat.svg" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4densbat.svg" + "><button type=button" + ">.svg</button></a> & <a href=" + "http:/" + "/atlas.brussels/ATLAS/Download/BBTphoneNIGHT4densbat.png" + " target=" + "_new" + " proposed_file_name=" + "BBTphoneNIGHT4densbat.png" + "><button type=button" + ">.png</button></a>") ;
	
